### Notes

\[^1]: Bhai Kalyana is the Sikh Sri Arjan sent into the hills; the raja is the raja of Mandi, whom Kalyana brought to the Guru (Ras 2.30 and 2.31).
\[^2]: The staff-bearers are chobdars, the ushers who walked before a raja.
\[^3]: Oankar: Guru Nanak's Dakhni Oankar in Raag Ramkali. Bhai Vir Singh gives the lines as the Granth has them: *lekhu na miṭaī he sakhī jo likhiā kartāri* (the writ the Creator has written is not erased, O friend) · *likhiā pheri na sakīai jiu bhāvī tiu sāri* (what is written cannot be turned back; as it pleases You, so take care of us) · *nadari terī sukhu pāiā nānak sabadu vīchāri* (by Your glance of grace, peace is found; Nanak, reflect on the shabad). Sri Guru Granth Sahib, Ang 937.
\[^4]: Prabhu: the Lord.
\[^5]: degh: the Guru's great cooking pot, and the food cooked in it for all · prashad: food blessed and shared.
\[^6]: Chandal: the caste the old order held lowest of all, charged with the burning grounds and with executions.
\[^7]: kos: about 3 km.

